 "problems": [
  "No Cliopatria row is owned by this batch; all 19 dossiers are new states (colonies, rebel regimes, states) with cliopatria_names [] and every keyframe new. Pages are shared across the commanderies, so lelang-commandery (7 pages) and xuantu-commandery (6) exceed the 2-5 page guidance on their own count.",
  "Cliopatria shapes of han-dynasty (-91..206), cao-cao (207..223), cao-wei (224..264) and western-jin (265..312) already contain the commanderies, daifang and the Gongsun land (bbox east edge 127-128E): ea-02/ea-03 must subtract them or the renderer must let the colony tint win. Cliopatria has no Han or Xin shape for 30..42.",
  "goguryeo (jk-02-b) needs a 314 gain from daifang-commandery, a 319 gain from xuantu-commandery, eastern-buyeo (not buyeo) as counterpart of the 22 gain, and a 494 (not 491) annexation of Buyeo; its 32-44 Nangnang events name han-dynasty where lelang-commandery now exists. dong-okjeo (jk-02-a) names lelang-commandery as counterpart of its -36 found, but no page opened places the Hamgyong coast under Lelang. The Ye and Okjeo are vassals of Lelang/Daifang from 245 (Goguryeo-Wei War page) but Goguryeo vassals in jk-02-b.",
  "Hamgyong (Xuantu's first seat) is left to nobody in 75 BCE (confidence 1); the colour agent should give the Han commanderies one family (china) and the occupation zones of 1945-48 the family korea; USAMGIK and SCA have no Cliopatria shapes and the republic-of-korea / democratic-people-s-republic-of-korea dossiers (jk-02-d) do not mention them.",
  "Many placements are readings at confidence 1-2 (Zhenfan, Xuantu after 75 BCE, Buyeo, Eastern Buyeo, Jeongan, Baekje restoration before 662, Sambyeolcho on Jindo); see the notes file. The validator warns only about unknown gazetteer place Seocheon and the missing murong-xianbei dossier.",
  "No infobox area was available for any of the 19 states, so the factor-of-two comparison against shapes.csv could not be made. Pages that failed: Jeongan_(state) and Baekje_revival_movement (replaced by Jeongan and Battle of Baekgang)."
 ]
}